From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] llama: load-time Q6_K requant of the UD Q8_0 projections + large-batch GEMM routing

Two coupled pieces that together convert the unsloth UD export's Q8_0
projection upcasts (attn_qkv/attn_gate/ssm_out/attn_q/attn_output, ~1.49 GB
of weight reads per decoded token, 39.7% of decode kernel time) into a
floor-safe decode win:

1. llama_model_loader requantizes the five families to Q6_K at load
   (~300 MB/token of decode traffic removed; exact-suffix matching; same
   ggml_quantize_chunk path as llama-quantize; conversion verified
   byte-identical across loads; GGML_LOAD_REQUANT=0 restores stock bytes).
2. Plain (non-expert, non-head) Q6_K matmuls at batch >= 64 route to the
   fp16 dequant+GEMM path instead of MMQ: RDNA4 Q6_K MMQ tiles cost ~20%
   more than GEMM at prefill batch sizes, which broke the ranked prefill
   floor (0.9476) on the requant-only variant. The output head is excluded
   so logit arithmetic matches stock - including it makes the ppl reading
   noisy and biased low. GGML_Q6K_MMQ_MAX_BATCH overrides; 0 disables.

Same-binary toggles, pinned to device 0 like the ranked runner: decode
106.1-106.4 -> 109.6-109.8 tok/s; prefill -1.9% (vs -10% through MMQ);
gate-corpus ppl 3.9146/3.9148/3.9151/3.9167 over four loads (stock 3.9314,
band 3.9118-3.9511). Q5_1 variants and shexp coverage measured and
rejected - the perplexity landscape is non-additive; see the track README.
---
